# Review findings first

Do NOT implement the latest reviewer comment yet.

Read the current task contract, all review findings, HEAD implementation, and relevant tests.

Cluster findings into conceptual failure classes. For the newest finding, classify A–E (genuine / sibling / threat-model expansion / reject / invalid).

If that class has already appeared twice: STOP. Redesign the abstraction. Do not patch.

Return first with:

1. current invariant
2. root failure class
3. why prior fixes did not close the class
4. smallest abstraction that eliminates the class
5. behaviors deliberately removed
6. proposed state model
7. RED acceptance matrix
8. estimated complexity

Do not modify production code until that analysis is complete.
